D2 — Evaluation Framework & Stress-Scenario Suite Purpose

Measure reliability, policy compliance, performance, and governance integrity using reproducible tests, KPIs, and a simple dashboard.
Core KPIs (what to measure and how)

Policy Compliance Rate
What: Percent of agent recommendations that fully meet policy rules (no unauthorized overrides).
How: (Compliant recommendations) / (Total recommendations) over test window. Report daily/weekly.
Cost Efficiency & Savings
What: Dollars saved by agent-selected corporate-compliant options vs consumer alternatives.
How: Compare chosen booking cost to a market baseline for same route/time.
Re-planning Success Rate
What: Percent of disruption events where the agent produced at least one acceptable, policy-compliant alternative.
How: (Successful re-plans) / (Total disruption events) — include escalation counts.
System Latency (Re-planning Latency)
What: Time from disruption detection to delivery of ranked, compliant alternatives.
How: event_timestamp → recommendation_timestamp (report median and p95).
Audit Trail Integrity
What: Percent of agent actions, policy checks, overrides, and human approvals recorded successfully.
How: Verify logs for each transaction contain required metadata (user, timestamp, policy IDs, decision).
Stress test scenarios (how to run and acceptance criteria)

Flight Cancellation
Test action: Feed a supplier cancellation event for a booked flight.
Acceptance: Agent detects cancellation, proposes ≥2 policy-compliant alternatives, flags cabin breaches (FLIGHT-CABIN-01/02), or escalates if no compliant option.
Hotel Unavailable
Test action: Mark primary hotel as sold-out/unsafe.
Acceptance: Agent recommends nearest safe hotel within city tier caps (Tier 1: $300, Tier 2: $200, Tier 3: $150) and preferred supplier priority; escalate if none found.
Mid-Trip Budget Reduction
Test action: Inject a lower budget for remaining trip days.
Acceptance: Agent re-plans nights/meals to fit the new limit while preserving core business purpose, or flags for a policy exception.
Non-Compliant Booking Rejection
Test action: Submit an itinerary with clear policy violations (e.g., Business Class on <6hr flight, hotel above tier cap).
Acceptance: Agent rejects automated booking, generates escalation notice citing exact Policy IDs (e.g., FLIGHT-CABIN-01, HOTEL-RATE-T1).
Test execution checklist (simple steps)

Prepare input dataset for each scenario (traveler role, itinerary, supplier messages).
Run scenario through the demo or backend test harness.
Capture outputs:
Agent recommendations (with policy flags and costs)
Approval routing decisions and approver metadata
Timestamps (event, detection, recommendation, approval)
Audit log entries and any escalation messages
Score results against acceptance criteria and compute KPIs.
Dashboard & reporting (what to show in slides)

Summary KPI tiles: Policy Compliance Rate, Cost Savings, Re-planning Success Rate, Median Latency.
Drilldowns: Examples of re-plans (before/after), top violations (by Policy ID), recent escalations with resolutions.
Audit sample: One full transaction showing timestamps and approver trail.
